From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:39:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk: USXGMII/LynxI PCS and XFI T-PHY updates for MT7988

Update the MediaTek USXGMII PCS driver (rate adaptation, 10GBase-R/
5GBase-R/USXGMII handling), the LynxI PCS (SGMII) driver, and the XFI
T-PHY driver for the NETSYS v3 ethernet driver. The XFI T-PHY
instance struct moves to a shared header (linux/phy/phy-mtk-xfi-
tphy.h) so the PCS drivers can drive the XFI T-PHY helpers directly,
and a CTLE validity check is added for 10G link tuning; the PCS and
T-PHY changes are interdependent, so they are carried as one patch.
Exports mtk_usxgmii_pcs_get/put for the ethernet driver. Pairs with
the mtk_eth_soc NETSYS v3 patch.

Signed-off-by: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
